:'''Huanxi:''' Perhaps you should know that Miss Bailu's path to becoming a high elder was neither in compliance with proper protocol nor of her own volition &mdash; everything was a result of the stubbornness of her predecessor &mdash; Dan Feng. His hubris and tyranny brought about the end of the Luofu's high elder succession.
:'''Huanxi:''' The Preceptors heard of Master Dan Heng's return, and were uncertain whether it constituted good or ill fortune. However, many have surmised that the Luofu's high elder succession tradition will soon be back in force. If true, that is indeed something worth celebrating.
:'''Huanxi:''' Whether we find another suitable candidate in accordance with the laws of our people... or have you take up the position anew &mdash; everything can still be mended.
:'''Huanxi:''' But, if Master Dan Heng were to hand everything over to Miss Bailu, it could lead to great upheavals on the horizon. No good would come of it for her.
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Another suitable candidate? Who does the Vidyadhara hope for?
::'''Huanxi:''' Hehe, such a major matter as this is naturally up to the Preceptor elders. I couldn't possibly say.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} I don't think she even wants to be the High Elder.
::'''Huanxi:''' I've been a maid here for twelve years now, and was with my mistress every day as she studied medicine and received tutelage. I've witnessed her countless escapes, and the inevitable unwilling returns.
::'''Huanxi:''' As far as the Xianzhou is concerned, children like her enjoy a charmed and happy childhood. But as a high elder in nothing but name alone, Miss Bailu is highly restricted in her actions and has no freedom or say about her own life.
::'''Huanxi:''' I can't bear it! Your Highness, please, think about this poor child!
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Shouldn't you ask Bailu herself about this?
::'''Huanxi:''' Miss Bailu is young, naive, and easily manipulated by others. I worry that under the pressure of others, she would be convinced into taking up too great a burden.
::'''Dan Heng:''' I understand your concern... but I have nothing more to say on the matter at present.
::'''Huanxi:''' Then I will bid my farewell.
::'''Huanxi:''' Master Dan Heng, whether you choose to meet Miss Bailu or go with me to see the Preceptor elders, I will be waiting for you by the ferry leading to Scalegorge Waterscape.
::----
::'''Dan Heng:''' I haven't even set eyes on Bailu, and people are already urging me not to meet her...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Finally, we can learn about Dan Heng's past!
:::'''Dan Heng:''' ...You've been spending too much time with March.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Should I keep this a secret from the others?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' No need. March will find out sooner or later.
::'''Dan Heng:''' You know that I'm a descendant of the Luofu Vidyadhara. In Scalegorge Waterscape, you witnessed my... "secret strength," as March would call it...
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...yet that power stems from Dan Feng &mdash; my previous incarnation. He altered the process of high elder succession, plunging everything into catastrophe... ultimately, he suffered the punishment of molting rebirth.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Based on the physiological principles of Vidyadhara reincarnation, I ought to have been an entirely new entity... and in view of the law, all crimes from my previous incarnation should have been wiped clean...
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...but in reality, I was locked up in The Shackling Prison at birth. Even after I was released and left the Xianzhou, my high elder past and Dan Feng's {{Rubi|enemies|Blade}} pursued me like a haunting shadow.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Now, I plan to face that shadow. In order to make amends, I want to repair the Ambrosial Arbor's seal... and visit the high elder, to see what more I can do.
::'''Dan Heng:''' The starskiff's ready. Let's go.
::----

