===Find the Ferryman and head to the Alchemy Commission delve together{{subst:void|<!--202060103-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Exalting Sanctum|update|Dan Heng's homecoming seems to be a big ordeal, requiring notice to be delivered to the Luofu's Six Charioteers and the Vidyadhara elders... Seeing as Dan Heng already made travel arrangements, you should go with him. It won't do for you to just use a Space Anchor to teleport to the Alchemy Commission alone.<br />Dan Heng never intended to conceal his Vidyadhara heritage, and this might explain why he possesses such a magnanimous demeanor nowadays. Yet, the Vidyadhara's attitude towards his return remains to be seen...}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
----
:'''??:''' The rumors are true &mdash; you really are back...
:'''Luying:''' I'm healer Luying of the Alchemy Commission &mdash; I'm a Vidyadhara too, as you can see. I'd heard the reincarnation of the great sinner has returned to the Luofu... and wanted to offer some advice.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Oh?
:'''Luying:''' Leave this troubled place immediately.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Looks like the Vidyadhara aren't big fans of yours.
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...I'm not surprised in the slightest. What does the Alchemy Commission want, then?
::'''Luying:''' Return to being a Nameless &mdash; stay out of the high elder succession.
::'''Luying:''' The Luofu Vidyadhara have finally recovered from Dan Feng's grievous sins, and were blessed with a compassionate and caring high elder in Bailu... none of this was easy. Your return has stirred up resentment and ambition among the Preceptors, and threatens our situation.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you here about the high elder succession, too?
::'''Luying:''' Certainly! Miss Bailu has weathered nothing but criticism since she was granted the title, but the Alchemy Commission firmly believes that girl to be a precious diamond in the rough. She is compassionate, kind, and a hundred times better than Dan Feng.
::'''Luying:''' Moreover, Dan Feng selected her as high elder, making her the leader of the Luofu Vidyadhara. Fate chose her as our sovereign, and we bowed down before that destiny.
::'''Luying:''' Now that you're back, everything has changed. The Preceptors are starting to think of finding other candidates, which means nothing but trouble for Miss Bailu.
:'''Dan Heng:''' I have no intention of threatening Bailu's position.
:'''Luying:''' You may have a clear conscience, but even so... As long as you remain on the Luofu, invisible forces will try to coerce you. Leave now. It's the best outcome for everyone involved.
:'''Luying:''' Do not repeat the mistakes of a past life in this one. Farewell.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Request an audience with the high elder and meet the messenger{{subst:void|<!--202060111-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Alchemy Commission|update|It seems the way home isn't comprised of polite greetings but people urging Dan Heng to turn back. Perhaps his return to the Xianzhou Luofu might not be the happiest affair...<br />Seeing how many people can recognize him with the barest mention, this might have to do with his revealed identity. This doesn't seem like something the usually circumspect Dan Heng is used to.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Hello, what brings you two here? The wind and waves are restless around Lunarescent Depths today.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Even you came to dissuade me from visiting the high elder, General?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha, this encounter was not of my making. I've been recuperating in the Alchemy Commission under the Dragon Lady's care &mdash; our paths have merely crossed...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' ...but your question would suggest that there are others interested in dissuading you from such a venture.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Yes &mdash; many. Each with their own agenda in mind.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's just a quick meeting. What's the big deal?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Matters that concern the rise and fall of the Vidyadhara will inevitably attract certain parties &mdash; those that would work circumstances to their advantage. Be it Dan Feng, the Preceptors, or the Alchemy Commission that trained the Dragon Lady...
:{{tx}}
----
----
:'''Jing Yuan:''' A chance meeting is a gift from fate. Why don't I help you to fathom their intent, then?
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Vidyadhara elders want to choose a new High Elder.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha, the power struggle between the Preceptors and their High Elder is a tale as old as time. And someone as powerful as Dan Feng, who was completely beyond their control, was enough for them to harbor a hidden rage.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' The elders used to have a small say in appointing the new High Elder. Who could have imagined that Dan Feng would pick his own successor? And yet, that is precisely what happened, and all they could do was accept the result.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Now that Dan Heng has arrived, the elders see yet another chance &mdash; how could they let it go?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Pretty bold of them!
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' Haha! Us outsiders should not judge the laws of the Vidyadhara.
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' The Preceptors have been suppressed for some time now &mdash; they will inevitably try to overturn the situation.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Seems reasonable!
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' The Dragon Lady has no power and Dan Feng is a criminal. One can understand their desire for a new high elder.
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' The Preceptors have been suppressed for some time now &mdash; they will inevitably try to overturn the situation.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} The Alchemy Commission hopes that Bailu can stay on as High Elder.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' These people speak of "legitimacy." They believe that Bailu was chosen as heir apparent by the previous High Elder, and that unless she were to commit a terrible sin, the Preceptors should have no right whatsoever to choose again.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' The Healer Lady has draconic features and scarcely believable therapeutic abilities. Some regard this as evidence that she is the High Elder. But the Preceptors are fixated on strength, and are unwilling to accept her...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Now that Dan Feng's reincarnation has shown a command over the vast marine expanse of Lunarescent Depths, those longing to keep the traditional bequeathal of the High Elder feel increasingly uneasy.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Very conservative of them!
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' After Dan Feng's abdication, they fought against the Preceptors and saved Bailu's dignity. They demonstrated a true devotion.
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' These folks aren't the type to just let it go.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Very reasonable!
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' Before Dan Heng arrived, everything was quiet as a windless lake. In that regard, it is understandable that they want to get rid of him.
:::'''Jing Yuan:''' These folks aren't the type to just let it go.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} General, what do you think about this?
::'''Jing Yuan:''' It is an internal affair of the Vidyadharas. As long as it does not disturb the peace aboard the Luofu, it does not involve the general of the Cloud Knights.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Nevertheless, as a friend, let me remind you of one thing. So long as Dan Heng and Bailu, with their respective High Elder powers and titles, both remain on the Luofu, the Vidyadhara will never cease their internal strife. This is not to say that either of you are to blame.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' It's getting late. You are headed to repair the Arbor's seal at Scalegorge Waterscape, and visit the High Elder, no? Farewell, for now. I should start taking this business of rest and recuperation a little more seriously.
::----

